        "text": "Finally, let's turn to cryptocurrencies, which work very differently compared to fiat currency. They are digital currencies in which transactions are verified and records maintained by blockchain technology using cryptography rather than by centralized authorities. This is what sets cryptocurrencies apart from the Digital currencies in PayPal and other digital banking apps that are operated by centralized organizations. A good cryptocurrency will be decentralized, meaning it has no owner and no one person or entity has control over it. While governments can unilaterally change the underlying rules of fiat money, cryptocurrencies should theoretically maintain an even playing field and consistent sets of rules.",
